WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.872
Meteoectasis. A word for the impact that leaves no trace of the impact.

2
00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:14.415
Two bodies. One is much larger than the other, and it is on a collision course.

3
00:00:14.415 --> 00:00:22.990
The literature calls this accretion. But accretion is a word about quantity, not about state.

4
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:29.294
Above the latent heat of fusion, the smaller body melts completely.

5
00:00:29.294 --> 00:00:36.924
It expands, it loses its mechanical integrity, and it becomes part of a fluid.

6
00:00:36.924 --> 00:00:46.301
This dilatation is the ektasis. It is what allows the material to mix, instead of remaining an inclusion.

7
00:00:46.301 --> 00:00:54.424
Once both are in the same molten reservoir, mixing proceeds on the timescale of the reservoir.

8
00:00:54.424 --> 00:01:02.553
The impactor loses its geochemical identity. Its atoms are no longer distinguishable.

9
00:01:02.553 --> 00:01:10.124
The target survives, and its composition has changed. This is meteoectasis.

10
00:01:10.124 --> 00:01:19.101
This is not new physics. The physics is in the literature. What is missing is the word for the state.

11
00:01:19.101 --> 00:01:28.288
And the word earns its keep where isotopic signatures have to be explained: Earth and Moon share one.

12
00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:38.085
The paper states its own defeat condition. If the distinction predicts nothing, the term should be withdrawn.

13
00:01:38.085 --> 00:01:44.316
Meteoectasis. Brisecom, October 2026.
